                <invention-title lang="de">SYSTEME UND VERFAHREN ZUM ANBRINGEN UND ABDICHTEN VON ENDVERSCHLÜSSEN AN BEHÄLTERN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SYSTÈMES ET PROCÉDÉS POUR L'APPLICATION ET L'ÉTANCHÉITÉ DE FERMETURES D'EXTRÉMITÉ SUR DES RÉCIPIENTS</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SYSTEMS AND METHODS FOR THE APPLICATION AND SEALING OF END CLOSURES ON CONTAINERS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A sealing system for hermetically sealing a closure (51) to a container (60) comprises:a die assembly (300) comprising:a die (80) having a positioning portion (90) configured to retain a disc (50) and a die opening (98) adjacent the positioning portion (90); andat least one sealing member (40) configured to provide heat to seal the disc (50) to the container (60); anda mandrel assembly (200) comprising:an outer mandrel (210) comprising an extending portion (212) which is sized to fit within an inner circumference of the positioning portion; andan inner mandrel (220) configured to translate through an inner circumference of the extending portion (212) of the outer mandrel (210) and the die opening (98), characterized in that:the system further comprises an ejector (30) disposed within an inner circumference of the inner mandrel (220),wherein at least the outer mandrel (210) is configured to translate a first distance in a first time period,wherein the inner mandrel (220) and the ejector (30) are configured to translate a second distance in a second time period,wherein the inner mandrel (220) is configured to retract a third distance in a third time period and wherein the ejector does not retract during said third time period,wherein the ejector (30) is configured to retract the third distance in a fourth time period which occurs later than the third time period, andwherein each of the first distance, the second distance, and the third distance are different from each other.</p>
            </abstract>
